{"id": "EUVD-2026-96556", "enisaUuid": "4c174019-3f1e-3c38-bbbe-bbcc9538bad8", "description": "JeecgBoot through 3.9.5 contains a missing authorization vulnerability that allows low-privileged authenticated users to create message templates by calling POST /sys/message/sysMessageTemplate/add. Attackers holding only minimal roles can insert arbitrary notification templates with chosen codes and content into the shared sys_sms_template library used for system, e-mail, SMS and IM notifications.", "datePublished": "2026-10-10T21:49:16", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-18T11:53:08", "baseScore": 5.3, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:N/VI:L/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/AnkesKasty/cve-request-poc/blob/a7b6d1423555812d8efa26c91c5d0683164b31e5/JeecgBoot/poc_c089_messagetemplate_add.py", "https://github.com/jeecgboot/JeecgBoot/blob/e3b9dc0aefe1943d9772b026f64ed671a7c82802/jeecg-boot/jeecg-module-system/jeecg-system-biz/src/main/java/org/jeecg/modules/message/controller/SysMessageTemplateController.java#L82-L86", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/jeecgboot-through-3.9.5-missing-authorization-via-sysmessagetemplate-add-endpoint"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-108617", "GHSA-9hw5-pj63-xrrf"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.24, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "ba3a2d15-bc88-304c-9999-a994174c760a", "product": {"name": "JeecgBoot", "vendor": {"name": "n/a"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22643.9.5"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "674cdca2-931b-3f7c-94e7-b6446dc554e1", "vendor": {"name": "jeecgboot"}}], "isExploited": false}